==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|perturben|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|perturber|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|perturbare||throw into confusion, confuse, disorder, disturb|lang=la}}, from {{m|la|per||through}} + {{term|lang=la|turbare||to confuse, disturb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-perturb.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)b|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[disturb]]; to bother or unsettle.
# {{context|physics|lang=en}} To slightly modify the motion of an object.
# {{context|astronomy|lang=en}} To modify the motion of a body by exerting a gravitational force.
# {{context|mathematics|lang=en}} To modify slightly, such as an equation or value.

====Derived terms====
* [[perturbation]]
* [[perturbative]]

